From 627930a25108c8d57db182f07dfdaa543bafac19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarkNikGr <mitakidisnikos@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:05:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/ca0132: add Sound Blaster AE-9 support

Add support for the Creative Sound Blaster AE-9 (PCI 1102:0010,
subsystem 1102:0071).  The card has two CA0132 codecs on one PCI
function, an ES9038Q2M headphone DAC, a SABRE9006 line-out DAC and an
external Audio Control Module (ACM) with a volume knob, a dB display
and buttons.

The driver replays the Windows bring-up sequence over the BAR2 command
engine: DSP master-control and loader setup, ASI/PLL, DAC and GPIO
configuration, the 8051 router hooks and the output-connect overlay
(request_firmware("ae9-dsp-output-overlay.bin")).  It also implements
the ACM UART protocol (115200 8N1, sysex frames) for the knob, display,
output switching and the SBX light, exposes the shared Headphone+LO
volume with 1 dB steps, adds the AE-9 mixer controls (including Direct
Mode and the HP/Speaker auto-detect gate), and brings up capture on the
secondary codec (line-in, S/PDIF) and, with ae9_capture=1, the main
codec microphone.

The card needs the HDA-core posted-write flush from the preceding
patch; without it probing hard-locks the machine.

Based on the out-of-tree sb-ae9 work.  The AE-9 protocol and the
auto-detect/shared-volume changes were developed on the same hardware
by s3boun3t (https://github.com/s3boun3t/ae9_build).

Signed-off-by: DarkNikGr <mitakidisnikos@gmail.com>
